# Win/Loss Log: Q1 2026 — Overview

## Summary
- **Total opportunities**: 12
- **Wins**: 7 (58.3% win rate)
- **Losses**: 4
- **No decision**: 1 (healthcare client, budget freeze)
- **Average deal size**: $485K

## Wins ($2.42M total)

| Deal | Value | Competitor | Key Win Factor |
|------|-------|-----------|----------------|
| Energy Cloud Migration | $620K | Accenture | Speed (16 weeks vs 9 months) |
| Healthcare Oracle ERP | $720K | Deloitte | Oracle specialization |
| Retail Analytics | $340K | Slalom | Pre-built dashboards |
| Bank Cybersecurity | $180K | Coalfire | Business-risk focus |
| Manufacturing SAP | $890K | IBM | Fixed-price certainty |
| Healthcare Salesforce | $250K | Cognizant | Nearshore cost advantage |
| SaaS Managed Services | $420K/yr | Rackspace | Scale-with-me model |

## Losses ($2.65M total)

| Deal | Value | Winner | Key Loss Factor |
|------|-------|--------|-----------------|
| Auto OEM Cloud | $1.2M | McKinsey | Brand prestige |
| State Gov ERP | $450K | Local incumbent | 10-year relationship |
| Insurance Data | $680K | Palantir | AI hype narrative |
| Children's Hospital Security | $320K | Boutique (2-person) | Price (40% lower) |

## Patterns

### Why We Win
1. Speed to value (shorter timelines)
2. Domain specialization (Oracle, manufacturing)
3. Pre-built accelerators (demonstrated POCs)
4. Fixed-price certainty (reduces executive anxiety)
5. Flexible engagement models (month-to-month options)

### Why We Lose
1. **Brand prestige** at Fortune 500 (McKinsey, Big 4)
2. **Incumbent relationships** in public sector
3. **AI hype** when selling to non-technical C-suite
4. **Price** when no lean option offered

## Action Items
- [ ] Build "Apex Elite" tier for Fortune 500
- [ ] Create public sector capture team (18-month horizon)
- [ ] Add AI/ML narrative to all data proposals
- [ ] Develop lean/premium team options for all templates
